      "value": "@{5f2dea8d22470972dc58e995|full_name}:  All of the issues Kizzy listed happen regardless of host. \nAdditionally, dropbox officially supports video streaming from their platform and according to dropbox support there is NO LIMIT on the number of concurrent users that can view a video  as long as you don't exceed your bandwidth allowance. The bandwidth allowance varies depending on your plan, and the allowance is PER FILE, not per account. On my plan that limit is 400GB(bytes, not bits) PER FILE which means I would need 100 people simultaneously watching a 4GB video file in order to exceed that file's bandwidth limit. Yet somehow I still experience the issues that Kizzy described with only myself and one other person in the instance.\nSorry, you can't just write this off with \"works on my machine\".",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
